In src/todo-store.js, at the text `export function readTodos(cwd) {
  throw new Error('not implemented')
}`: Replace with an implementation that reads todoPath(cwd): if !fs.existsSync(p) return []; otherwise JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(p, 'utf8')), and throw new Error(`${STORE_FILENAME} is not a valid todo store`) if the parsed value is not an array.

In src/todo-store.js, at the text `export function writeTodos(cwd, todos) {
  throw new Error('not implemented')
}`: Replace with: fs.writeFileSync(todoPath(cwd), JSON.stringify(todos, null, 2) + '\n', 'utf8'). Return nothing.

In src/todo-store.js, at the text `export function addTodo(cwd, text) {
  throw new Error('not implemented')
}`: Replace with: throw new Error('todo text is required') if text is not a string or text.trim() is empty; read the current todos, compute id = highest existing numeric id (or 0) + 1, build the record { id, text: text.trim(), done: false }, push it onto the array, call writeTodos(cwd, todos), and return the new record.

In src/todo-store.js, at the text `export function completeTodo(cwd, id) {
  throw new Error('not implemented')
}`: Replace with: read the todos, findIndex(t => t.id === id); return false if the index is -1. Otherwise set that record's done to true (leaving id and text untouched), call writeTodos(cwd, todos) and return true. It must be idempotent — calling it twice still returns true.

In src/todo-store.js, at the text `export function removeTodo(cwd, id) {
  throw new Error('not implemented')
}`: Replace with: read the todos, findIndex(t => t.id === id); return false if the index is -1. Otherwise splice the record out of the array, call writeTodos(cwd, todos) and return true.

In src/todo-store.js, at the text `export function todoPath(cwd) {
  return `${cwd}/${STORE_FILENAME}`
}`: Replace the body with `return path.join(cwd, STORE_FILENAME)`, and add `import fs from 'node:fs'` and `import path from 'node:path'` as the first two lines of the file (above the leading comment) so the store resolves paths portably instead of concatenating a slash.

